# Pipe-vs-dot precedence: dot binds tighter than pipe
# `d.x | f` parses as `(d.x) | f`, not `d.(x | f)`
# If dot did not bind tighter, `d.(x | f)` would key into d with the result of `x | f`,
# which would be a different value or an error.
[
  d: [x: 5]
  add1: [fn [n] [+ n 1]]
]

d.x | add1
=== out
Int(6)
